{% doc %}
  Per-brand free-shipping progress, in the cart.

  THE CART IS THE ONLY PLACE THIS ARITHMETIC IS REAL. Shipping on Collective is
  charged per supplier, so a whole-cart "spend $50 for free shipping" would be
  the wrong number in both directions — too low for someone buying across three
  brands, meaningless for someone one item away from a single brand's threshold.
  Only the cart knows the per-vendor subtotal, so only the cart can say "you are
  $12.53 from free shipping on Sweet Bamboo" and have it be true.

  It also catches the shopper at the one moment adding something is easy: they
  have already decided to buy.

  WHAT IT REFUSES TO SAY. Twenty-five suppliers have a threshold; six of those
  have one their own catalogue cannot reach, and nine more get MORE expensive as
  items are added. Those fifteen render nothing at all. Inviting a bigger basket
  from a scaling supplier costs us money, and quoting a gap nobody can close is
  a promise with nothing behind it — measured, not assumed, by the shipping
  agent in `vendor_shipping`.

  UNITS. Cart money in Liquid is CENTS; the threshold metafield is DOLLARS.
  Everything below works in cents and converts once, at the end.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign vendors = ''
  for line in cart.items
    assign v = line.product.vendor
    if v != blank
      assign probe = '~' | append: v | append: '~'
      unless vendors contains probe
        assign vendors = vendors | append: '~' | append: v | append: '~'
      endunless
    endif
  endfor
  assign vendor_list = vendors | split: '~~'
-%}

{%- capture rows -%}
  {%- for raw_vendor in vendor_list -%}
    {%- assign vendor = raw_vendor | remove: '~' -%}
    {%- if vendor == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      # Subtotal for THIS brand only, in cents.
      assign vendor_cents = 0
      for line in cart.items
        if line.product.vendor == vendor
          assign vendor_cents = vendor_cents | plus: line.final_line_price
        endif
      endfor

      assign vs = nil
      for entry in shop.metaobjects.vendor_shipping.values
        if entry.vendor.value == vendor
          assign vs = entry
          break
        endif
      endfor
    -%}

    {%- if vs -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign shape = vs.shape.value
        assign msg = nil
        assign pct = 0
        assign show_link = false
        # Reset per vendor. Liquid `assign` is function-scoped across the whole
        # loop, so without this a second supplier with no threshold would render
        # the previous supplier's gap as its own.
        assign gap_amount = nil
        assign gap_vendor = nil
        # `won` is narrower than `pct == 100` on purpose. The 'flat' and 'free'
        # shapes also sit at 100%, but those are standing facts about a supplier,
        # not something the shopper just achieved by filling their basket. Only
        # a threshold they actually crossed earns the loud treatment; using it
        # everywhere would make the celebration mean nothing.
        assign won = false

        if shape == 'threshold' and vs.reachable.value
          # Rounded before use: free_threshold is a decimal metafield and Liquid
          # arithmetic on those goes float.
          assign threshold_cents = vs.free_threshold.value | times: 100 | round
          if vendor_cents >= threshold_cents
            assign msg = 'Free shipping on ' | append: vendor
            assign pct = 100
            assign won = true
          else
            assign gap = threshold_cents | minus: vendor_cents
            assign gap_money = gap | money
            assign msg = nil
            assign gap_amount = gap_money
            assign gap_vendor = vendor
            assign pct = vendor_cents | times: 100 | divided_by: threshold_cents
            # A bar that starts empty reads as "you have done nothing". Every
            # cart reaching this line has already spent something, so the fill
            # never sits below a visible sliver.
            if pct < 6
              assign pct = 6
            endif
            assign show_link = true
          endif

        elsif shape == 'flat'
          assign msg = 'Anything else from ' | append: vendor | append: ' ships with no extra shipping.'
          assign pct = 100

        elsif shape == 'free'
          assign msg = 'Free shipping on ' | append: vendor | append: '.'
          assign pct = 100
        endif
      -%}

      {%- if msg or gap_amount -%}
        <li class="aj-ship-progress__row{% if won %} aj-ship-progress__row--won{% endif %}{% if gap_amount %} aj-ship-progress__row--gap{% endif %}">
          {%- if gap_amount -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              THE NUMBER IS THE ASK, so it is the biggest thing here. This was
              one sentence of 15px body text carrying "$28.00" in the middle of
              it, at the same weight as the shipping policy — the one figure
              that decides whether somebody adds another item was the least
              visible thing in the block.

              Purple, not the yellow the earned state uses. Yellow is this
              brand's "you got something" and this is "here is something to
              do" — reusing the win colour for an unmet target makes the actual
              win mean less when it lands two seconds later.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="aj-ship-progress__msg">
              <span class="aj-ship-progress__gap">{{ gap_amount }}</span>
              <span class="aj-ship-progress__gap-tail">
                more from {{ gap_vendor }} and shipping is <strong>free</strong>
              </span>
            </p>
            <div class="aj-ship-progress__track" role="presentation">
              <div class="aj-ship-progress__fill" style="width: {{ pct }}%"></div>
            </div>
            {%- if show_link -%}
              {%- assign vendor_key = 'vendor-' | append: gap_vendor | handleize -%}
              <a class="aj-ship-progress__link" href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/{{ vendor_key }}">
                See everything from {{ gap_vendor }} &rarr;
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <p class="aj-ship-progress__msg">
              {%- if won -%}
                <span class="aj-ship-progress__tick" aria-hidden="true">&check;</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {{ msg }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if rows contains '<li' -%}
  <ul class="aj-ship-progress" role="list">{{ rows }}</ul>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-ship-progress {
    /* Top margin because this block sits directly beneath the last line item's
       quantity stepper, and with none the banner collided with it — a filled
       yellow bar touching a bordered control reads as one broken widget rather
       than two things. */
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__msg {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__link { text-decoration: underline; }

  .aj-ship-progress__track {
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.12);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.7);
    /* No transition: the cart re-renders on change rather than animating in
       place, so a transition would only ever play on first paint. */
  }

  /* --- the unmet target ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap {
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    border-radius: 12px;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__msg {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /* The figure the whole block exists to communicate. */
  .aj-ship-progress__gap {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    margin-inline-end: 0.3rem;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__gap-tail { font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__track {
    height: 8px;
    background: rgb(122 63 160 / 0.15);
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__fill {
    background: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    transition: width 0.35s ease;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__link {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .aj-ship-progress__row--gap .aj-ship-progress__fill { transition: none; }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
